		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4374&amp;p=37489#p37489"><![CDATA[
Question for the devs<br><br>What is known about the "silent DMR" issue anyway? <br><br>I rummaged through the forum looking for conversations on this "silent DMR" issue. It's really bugging me as it is consistently ruining every single one of my QSOs because i keep missing transmissions.<br><br>I've been doing some tests and this is the info/questions i have:<br><ul><li>Is the issue restricted to transmissions from MMDVM?</li></ul><ul><li>Does the issue arise with specific callers only?</li></ul><ul><li>Is it a DM1701/TYT issue or is it a general OpenGD77 issue?</li></ul><ul><li>Was it present on the latest stable?</li></ul>Regarding the first, I haven't been able to reproduce the issue on a normal repeater around here. Transmissions seem get through just fine.<br>Also, I am yet to reproduce the issue listening to my MMDVM using an SDR, and see if both go silent/helicoptering.<br>For the note: my hotspot is duplex with 2 timeslots<br><br>Regarding the second. It disproportionally affects transmissions from a specific fellow ham. When monitoring the anchored TG, other hams seem to be heard ok. The issue is less frequent. Also, this fellow ham is the one I talk to the most. So perhaps TXing makes the issue more likely?<br><br>Regarding the third, I don't know. I don't have other OpenGD77s.<br><br><br><br>Random ideas/observations:<ul><li>When the issue "kicks in", restarting does NOT solve it. It keeps losing transmissions</li></ul><ul><li>TXing seems to make the issue more likely (change of behavior based on temperature)</li></ul>I am thinking of getting on the code and compile it and run educated tests on my hardware because as it stands, it's become almost unusable.<br><br>Is there any test you'd want me to conduct? How could I help?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6012">EA4IAU</a> — Sat Jun 14, 2025 9:11 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
